{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"8272ded1e2b040d195bb8040a930cfdbc911680b84fb68d2e620e9d6d226732d","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_0001367fa666c26cf07ba8613a02be5b3121fa7aca601d516b733ee50cd00271","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technically sound extension of CCA to a deep generative framework, with a clear derivation of the variational lower bound and a well-motivated private-variable variant. The experimental evaluation is comprehensive, covering three distinct domains and a strong set of baselines. However, the lack of statistical significance testing and the omission of certain implementation details (such as the number of Monte Carlo samples and specific hyperparameters) limit the reproducibility and the statistical rigor of the reported results.","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","paper_identity_sha256":"20c96de2d541434d2b452884881364c7b5da9f0ba89057c6cc81b9b405921229","prompt_identity_sha256":"8fed6708a43dd7348fb28bffd2eef7225ff4d721b2e6d83a0c17f52a43f5ed3d","raw_response_sha256":"34a2340aadde554f1dd1150198a3761ebfc69922bf7b080c413a9dbdb4ae05b8","request_identity_sha256":"1224accf3d9499105f4a029c3b92de4dea37ee5693840eb1c965d72c9319e3ef","reviewer_identity_sha256":"c1cd7c7fdd4a2cbeb45c2f21af982ad0f30bffae8ae148e3eba36479685cf360","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"b821e43be712e80f9ef8a1c1bd694e1cef6c4afedb10f9131936b7e1cfdffab5","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-010","SRC-011","SRC-012","SRC-013","SRC-014","SRC-015","SRC-016","SRC-017","SRC-018","SRC-020","SRC-021","SRC-022","SRC-023","SRC-024"],"review_text":"The proposed VCCA and VCCA-private models are mathematically well-formulated. The derivation of the variational lower bound (Equation 3) is correct and follows standard variational inference principles. The use of the reparameterization trick to enable stochastic gradient descent is appropriate for the intractable posterior. The extension to VCCA-private (Equation 13) correctly incorporates private variables into the joint distribution and the variational objective. The connection to multi-view autoencoders (MVAE) is clearly established by showing that VCCA reduces to MVAE in the limit of zero variance, which provides a strong conceptual grounding for the method.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-MET"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-030","SRC-031","SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-034","SRC-035","SRC-036","SRC-037","SRC-038","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The experimental design is robust, utilizing three distinct datasets (Noisy MNIST, XRMB, and MIR-Flickr) to validate the model across different domains (image-image, speech-articulation, and image-text). The choice of baselines is appropriate, including linear CCA, DCCA, DCCAE, contrastive loss, and MVAE. The evaluation metrics (classification error, phone error rate, and mAP) are standard for the respective tasks. The ablation study on dropout (Figure 6) and the analysis of private variables (Figure 8) provide useful insights into the model's behavior. However, the paper does not report the number of Monte Carlo samples (L) used in the experiments, which is a critical hyperparameter for the variational approximation.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-EXP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-032","SRC-033","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper provides some implementation details, such as the network architecture (number of layers and units) and the use of dropout. However, several key details are missing, which hinders full reproducibility. Specifically, the number of Monte Carlo samples (L) used for the variational approximation is not specified. The learning rate, batch size, and number of training epochs are also not provided. The paper mentions that the standard deviations of the observation models are tuned by grid search, but the range of values searched is not given. The code is not mentioned as being available, which is a common expectation for reproducibility in this field.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-REP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-028","SRC-029","SRC-036","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper compares VCCA and VCCA-private against a strong set of baselines, including linear CCA, DCCA, DCCAE, contrastive loss, and MVAE. These are all relevant and state-of-the-art methods for multi-view representation learning. The comparisons are fair, as all methods are evaluated on the same datasets and using the same evaluation metrics. The paper also discusses the relationship between VCCA and MVAE, providing a clear distinction between the two methods. The literature review is thorough, covering both classical and deep multi-view learning approaches.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-CMP"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-036","SRC-039","SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper reports mean performance metrics (error rates and mAP) but does not provide any statistical significance tests or confidence intervals. This is a significant limitation, as it is unclear whether the observed improvements over the baselines are statistically meaningful or due to random variation. The paper does not report the variance or standard deviation of the results across multiple runs, which is essential for assessing the robustness of the model. The lack of statistical rigor weakens the empirical claims of the paper.","subdimension_id":"QUAL-STA"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"73cc599ece362e6c97cc5ad731068cfbcdcfb88f29b1558e943d030e1dd0d21d","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","paper_ordinal":89,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"34a2340aadde554f1dd1150198a3761ebfc69922bf7b080c413a9dbdb4ae05b8","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"H1Heentlx","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"4e75e6fa22fc98b938be78abb73a4a487d36304d390f9aeff0c0001d6d7d96e1","request_identity_sha256":"1224accf3d9499105f4a029c3b92de4dea37ee5693840eb1c965d72c9319e3ef","role":"QUAL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v5","usage":{"completion_tokens":1299,"prompt_tokens":21291,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":22590},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"1224accf3d9499105f4a029c3b92de4dea37ee5693840eb1c965d72c9319e3ef","role":"QUAL","role_ordinal":0,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}